Hana: quick PSA — ran into a subtle UX problem in the Go generator sample where aggressive cancel/retry loops cause either duplicated partial tokens or the iterator to block. Wanted to dump notes and ask for a recommended onboarding pattern.

Rolf: thanks, can you share the minimal repro?

Hana: yes, minimal pattern:
```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 200*time.Millisecond)
defer cancel()
iter, err := client.Generate(ctx, req)
if err != nil { return "", err }
for t := range iter.Stream() { out += t }
return iter.Result(), nil // sometimes blocks if ctx canceled during handshake
```

Diego: we hit this in a microservice that does tight retries on mobile networks. Two failure modes we observed: (1) Result() blocks when the handshake goroutine never finishes; (2) repeated partial tokens when socket buffers get replayed on reconnects. Both often happen when a token refresh (401) or TCP reset occurs mid-handshake.

Hana: current workaround in my app: always create a new Generator per retry and use a small helper to consume/abort safely. That avoids the replay but increases latency and allocation. Example helper:
```go
func consumeWithCancel(ctx context.Context, it sdk.Iterator) (string, error) {
  tokCh := make(chan string, 8)
  done := make(chan struct{})
  go func() {
    for tk := range it.Stream() { tokCh <- tk }
    close(done)
  }()
  var out string
  for {
    select {
    case <-ctx.Done():
      // best-effort cleanup
      _ = it.Close(context.Background())
      return "", ctx.Err()
    case t := <-tokCh:
      out += t
    case <-done:
      return it.Result(), nil
    }
  }
}
```

Rolf: good pattern. From SDK side I propose: (A) add Iterator.Close(ctx) so callers can force cleanup; (B) add ResultWithContext(ctx) to avoid indefinite blocking; (C) doc guidance: "recreate Generator when doing tight cancel/retry loops".

Diego: plus a sample in quickstart comparing: generator-per-retry vs reuse-with-drain (include rough latency numbers). That helps users pick.

DocsBot: Filed issue #5384 "go-sdk: iterator Close/ResultWithContext + quickstart guidance for retry patterns" and added a checklist for samples + migration note.

CI-bot: PR incoming: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk-go/pull/322 (contains quickstart sample + iterator Close API; ci: flaky on darwin)

Hana: thanks — I'll wire the sample into onboarding and add a short FAQ entry about token-rotation-at-transport vs per-request refresh to reduce mid-handshake 401 races. Ping me for review on the PR.

Rolf: will review. Also let's add a tiny e2e that fuzzes mid-handshake cancels so we catch regressions.

Hana: agreed. closing this thread after PR merges. :rocket:
